,"scenes":[{"id":98497937254844,"name":"Cantautores de los setenta","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1970,"end":1983,"desc":"James Taylor se convierte, misteriosamente, en el prototipo del cantautor de los setenta; Carole King, Carly Simon y Don McLean, sobrevalorados. Las innovaciones llegan del oeste: Randy Newman y sus viñetas urbanas con fusión de estilos populares, Shawn Phillips, J.J. Cale y su estilo «laid-back», Gram Parsons, Emmylou Harris, Roger McGuinn, Jackson Browne (Late For The Sky) y, sobre todo, Tom Waits, discípulo de Beefheart y cronista de marginados (Swordfishtrombones, Rain Dogs). Excéntricos como Todd Rundgren y Annette Peacock; en Gran Bretaña, Peter Hammill, Anthony Moore, Richard Thompson, Robert Calvert, John Cale, Kevin Coyne, Elton John y los ex Beatles. El realismo de Bruce Springsteen, verdadero heredero de Woody Guthrie y del blues, y la escuela italiana de cantautores (De André, Guccini, Battisti, Sorrenti).","color":"#a3e635","family":"Folk y cantautores","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-70s"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":142313815256805,"artist":"Jim Croce","artist_id":134483241258940,"title":"I Got A Name","year":null,"ess":0,"yt":"O_BEFyNNIvM","kind":"s","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los setenta","scene_id":98497937254844,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-70s","chapters":["Sección 4.3"],"pages":[[1,87,null]]},{"id":187615596064536,"artist":"Jim Croce","artist_id":134483241258940,"title":"Time In A Bottle","year":null,"ess":0,"yt":"Q29sOLG8xGE","kind":"s","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Cantautores de los setenta","scene_id":98497937254844,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#songwriters-70s","c